.TH SLAYER\-EDITOR 1 "2026-10-14" "slayer-editor 0.4.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slayer\-editor \- lightweight code editor with an embedded terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slayer\-editor
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Slayer Editor
is a Qt\ 6 code editor with tabs, syntax highlighting, auto\-indentation,
auto\-closing pairs, find/replace and several color themes. The view can be
split Kate\-style into several panes that share the same document.
.PP
An embedded terminal (QTermWidget) can be docked on the left, top, right or
bottom of the window, or detached. Press
.B F5
to compile and run the current file: C, C++, Python, Rust, Go, JavaScript,
Java and shell scripts are supported out of the box.
.PP
When the matching language server is installed, Slayer Editor provides
diagnostics and completion over the Language Server Protocol (for example
.BR clangd ,
.BR pylsp ,
.BR rust\-analyzer ,
.BR gopls ) ,
and a visual debugger over the Debug Adapter Protocol
.RB ( gdb
for C/C++,
.B debugpy
for Python).
.PP
Any number of
.I FILE
arguments are opened in tabs on startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/slayer\-editor/slayer\-editor.conf
Per\-user settings (theme, fonts, toolbar, language servers and custom
symbols). Remove this file to restore the defaults.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_SCALE_FACTOR
Overrides the interface scale set in
.BR Settings\ \->\ Appearance .
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Wyllian Bezerra da Silva <wyllianbs@gmail.com>.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gdb (1),
.BR clangd (1)
